<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Export Board Data</title></head><body><table width='100%' border = '1' cellpadding='3' bgcolor='#CCECFF'><tr><td><B>Applicant</B></td><td>sudhir.kunnure@capgemini.com</td><td><B>Level</B></td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td><B>Status</B></td><td>Further Information Required</td><td><B>Lapse Date</B></td><td> </td></tr><tr><td><B>1st Sponsor</B></td><td>zankar.sheth@capgemini.com (Pending)</td><td><B>Renewal?</B></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td><B>2nd Sponsor</B></td><td>rinkesh.chhetia@capgemini.com (Pending)</td><td><B>Grade</B></td><td>D</td></tr><tr><td><B>SBU / GBL</B></td><td>DCX</td><td><B>BU</B></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><B>Region</B></td><td>Asia Pacific</td><td><B>Country</B></td><td>India</td></tr><tr><td><B>Gender</B></td><td>Male</td><td><B>Replaced?</B></td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2><B>Mandatory Training Completed</B></td><td colspan=2>No</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2><B>Mandatory Training Waived</B></td><td colspan=2>No</td></tr><tr><td colspan=4><B>Delivery & Market Development:</B><BR><div class="ExternalClass9B1B6BB62AF94E2EA73B481522A275B8"><div><ul><li>I have 18+ years of IT experience, delivering Solution Architecture ownership across insurance and banking domains.<br></li><li>At Grange Insurance, I defined and owned the UI solution architecture for agent-facing portals, aligning Figma design systems, API contracts, and React-based component framework.<br></li><li><div>I designed and governed a design-to-code UI automation framework, enabling generation of 20+ production UI pages and reducing development effort by 60–70%.<br></div></li><li><div><div>I established frontend architecture standards, covering accessibility (WCAG), performance, security, and code quality governance.</div></div></li><li><div><div>At Progressive Insurance, I owned UI modernization architecture, defining reusable component strategies and API-driven screen composition.<br></div></div></li><li><div><div>At SCB, I delivered enterprise UI architecture artefacts including solution diagrams, component models, integration flows, and non-functional requirement definitions.<br></div></div></li><li><div>I led teams of 6–10 engineers, performed architecture reviews, and enforced governance checkpoints.<br></div></li><li><div>I delivered architecture artefacts such as HLDs, LLDs, reference architectures, UI standards, and API-UI mapping specifications.<br></div></li></ul></div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=4><B>Capgemini Contribution:</B><BR><div class="ExternalClassADE24060FD1E4183A86A5C535E8E5327"><ul><li>​I support cross-account architecture excellence by performing UI and frontend solution architecture reviews for delivery teams outside my core assignment.<br></li><li>I provide architecture inputs for bids and proposals, defining UI modernization strategies, tooling accelerators, and delivery approaches.<br></li><li><div>I participate in Flying Squad–style technical interventions, resolving UI performance, accessibility, and architectural issues.<br></div></li><li><div>I conduct reference and consultation sessions to showcase reusable UI architecture patterns and accelerators to internal stakeholders.<br></div></li><li><div>I create and publish architecture PoVs on design-to-code automation, frontend governance, and scalable UI frameworks.<br></div></li><li><div><div>I actively share knowledge assets via KM portals, TMG-All, Yammer, and internal forums.<br></div></div></li><li><div><div>I mentor engineers and aspiring architects across accounts, strengthening Capgemini’s architecture capability and community.<br></div></div></li><li><div>I promote innovation and inclusion initiatives that support growth of the technical and architecture practice.<br></div></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=4><B>Thought Leadership:</B><BR><div class="ExternalClass47ADE979230747878FF827E020EB63E3"><ul><li>​I introduced design-to-code architecture patterns that convert Figma designs and API schemas into production-ready UI components.<br></li><li><div>I defined reusable frontend architecture patterns applied across insurance and banking clients, enabling consistent UI delivery.<br></div></li><li><div>I established API-driven UI composition models, improving separation of concerns between backend contracts and frontend rendering.<br></div></li><li><div>I applied modern frontend skills including React with TypeScript, state management modernization, and component-level governance.<br></div></li><li><div>I embedded accessibility-first architecture and automated quality controls (ESLint, Sonar, unit testing) as default architectural standards.<br></div></li><li><div><div>I created and shared architecture PoVs on UI automation, frontend scalability, and design system governance.<br></div></div></li><li><div>I enabled reuse of architectural patterns across multiple programs, reducing setup effort for new projects.<br></div></li><li><div>I shared insights through internal knowledge platforms and technical forums, promoting adoption of modern UI architecture practices.<br></div></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=4><B>Community Contribution:</B><BR><div class="ExternalClass9C767E716E6343E3888EF954F97B90E1"><ul><li>​I actively operate within the Architecture Practice, supporting capability growth through standardization of solution and UI architecture patterns.<br></li><li><div>I mentor engineers and aspiring architects, guiding them on architecture thinking, design trade-offs, and solution ownership.<br></div></li><li><div><div>I lead architecture knowledge-sharing sessions on UI automation, design systems, API-driven UI, and frontend governance.<br></div></div></li><li>I support architecture reviews and assurance activities, helping teams improve scalability, security, and maintainability.<br></li><li><div>I help develop future architects by sharing reference architectures, templates, and decision frameworks.<br></div></li><li><div><div>I hold an Azure Solution Architect certification, demonstrating alignment with industry-recognized architecture standards.<br></div></div></li><li><div>I actively participate in architecture community forums such as TMG-All, Yammer, and internal collaboration channels.<br></div></li><li>I promote continuous learning and innovation to strengthen the Architecture and Technical community.<br></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=4><B>Sponsor Comments:</B><BR> </td></tr></table><br style=�page-break-before: always�></body></html>